.TH "ROARK\-AGENT\-CONFIG\-RESOLVE" "1" "" "roark-agent-config-resolve" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-agent\-config\-resolve \- Resolve config for a session
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark agent\-config resolve
\fIkey\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
The call your agent makes at session start. Returns the config JSON for this session, with per\-session simulation recognition built in: when the session was originated by a Roark simulation (matched by caller number against the calls Roark has in flight), the STAGING revision is served for that session only, so Autoimprove candidates are tested on your real deployment. Real traffic always resolves to production; any recognition miss degrades to production too. On the first fetch of an unknown key, pass `defaults` (your baked\-in config): the key is registered and the defaults become revision 1. That makes integration a single call. Cache the response per session; do not fetch per turn.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/agent\-config/{key}/resolve
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIkey\fR
The key.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-defaults\fR \fI<value>\fR
Your baked\-in config. On the first fetch of an unknown key this registers the config and becomes revision 1, so integration is a single call. Ignored once the key exists. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR \fI<value>\fR
Session context. When the call was originated by a Roark simulation, Roark recognizes it here and serves the staging revision for this session only; real traffic always gets production. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-session.session\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
Your session or room identifier, for correlation. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-session.caller\-number\fR \fI<value>\fR
The number calling your agent (E.164). Required for simulation recognition. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-session.called\-number\fR \fI<value>\fR
The number your agent was reached on (E.164). Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
roark agent\-config resolve <key>
.fi
.RE
